Translation patch: local names in `Params::into_values` and `Params::into_positional`

Change: in `into_values`, the binding `Some(params)` becomes `Some(names)` and the loop variable `value` becomes `val`; in `into_positional`, the local `params` becomes `positional`, the bindings `Some(value)` become `Some(val)`, and the catch-all arm `params => Ok(params)` becomes `other => Ok(other)`.
Why: Aeneas bug (as in patch 59): the generated Lean names definitions by module path (`params.Params.Named`, `params.MissingNamedParameterError`, `value.Value.NULL`), and a local variable `params` (or `value`) shadows that prefix, so Lean reads `params.Params..` as a field projection on the local ("Invalid field `Params`").
Behaviour: Identical: renaming.

